title: Dashboard › Summary from FLO › What the three lines say and where they lead
route: /dashboard
intro: A compact card under the headline. FLO works three short lines out from the live demo data: who needs you and what is due soonest, which authorizations end within 7 days, and which denial deadlines fall this week. Each line has a link to the screen it is about. It is a recommendation for a person to check, not a payer fact, and it ignores the filters below it.
dir: TD
also: The wording and the numbers are computed each time. Nothing in the card is typed by hand.
---
start s1 "Open the Dashboard"
screen sc "Card 'Summary from FLO'\nSmall note: 'From today's demo data'\nThree lines, each with a link on the right"
agent a1 "FLO reads the requests, the Authorizations queue, the Case Manager ledger and the demo clock\nIt reads them again whenever any of them changes"

group gL1 "Line 1: who needs you and what is due soonest"
  decision d1 "Does any request need you?"
  screen l1 "'3 requests need you. Most urgent: I-2207 (Cardinal), recert due in 5 h.'\nThe one due first among the requests that wait on a person"
  screen l1n "'Nothing needs you right now.'"
  decision d1b "Is the request due soonest in the queue a different one?"
  screen l1s "Adds 'Due soonest: R-0988 (Beacon), review due in 3 h.'\nThe same answer as Ask FLO's 'What is due soonest?'"
  click k1 "Click 'Open I-2207'\n(or 'Open R-0988' when nothing needs you)"
end e1 "Authorizations case page of that request opens"
endgroup

group gL2 "Line 2: authorizations that end within 7 days"
  decision d2 "Does an approval on the Case Manager ledger end within 7 days?"
  screen l2 "'I-2193 has used 46 of 48 units and ends in 14 h. 3 more end within 7 days.'\nThe case that ends first, its units used of total, and how many more"
  screen l2n "'No authorization ends in the next 7 days.'"
  screen l2e "Adds '2 authorizations have already ended.' when an end date has passed"
  click k2 "Click 'Open Case Manager'"
endgroup

group gL3 "Line 3: denial deadlines this week"
  decision d3 "Does an open denial have a deadline within 7 days?"
  screen l3 "'4 denial deadlines fall this week. Nearest: D-3318 (Cardinal), peer-to-peer window, 36 h left.'"
  screen l3n "'No denial deadline falls this week.'"
  screen l3e "Adds '1 window has already closed.' when a deadline has passed"
  click k3 "Click 'Open Denial Intelligence'"
endgroup

wait w1 "The demo changes: Demo menu › Fast-forward 1 hour or 1 day, a payer reply from the request drawer, a request signed and sent, a draft answered"
process p1 "The lines are worked out again\nExample after a day: 'recert due now', 'ends in 2 days', '2 authorizations have already ended'"

goto g1 "Continues in: Authorizations › Case page › Ways in"
goto g2 "Continues in: Case Manager › Active cases › Tracker of every active case"
goto g3 "Continues in: Denial Intelligence › A denial opened"
goto g4 "Continues in: Global shell › Top bar › Ask FLO › What FLO answers"

s1 --> sc --> a1 --> d1
d1 -->|Yes| l1 --> d1b
d1 -->|No| l1n --> d1b
d1b -->|Yes| l1s --> k1
d1b -->|No| k1
k1 --> e1 --> g1
a1 --> d2
d2 -->|Yes| l2 --> l2e --> k2
d2 -->|No| l2n --> l2e
k2 --> g2
a1 --> d3
d3 -->|Yes| l3 --> l3e --> k3
d3 -->|No| l3n --> l3e
k3 --> g3
w1 --> p1 --> a1
l1s -.-> g4
